    <fr-refs>FR-11 (verify); grounds FR-01 (020), FR-02 (010), FR-09/FR-10 (030/031)</fr-refs>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    De-risk Phases 1–3 by confirming the operator-created schema inputs are LIVE in `spaarkedev1` before any r1 task builds against them. This is a READ-ONLY spike — NO schema change, NO code change. Produce ONE findings note under `projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/notes/` that downstream tasks (010, 020, 030) consume so they build against ground truth and read the `sprk_recordtype_ref` catalog **defensively** where it is dirty.

    Confirm, at minimum, via Dataverse MCP read tools (`describe`, `read_query`, `search`) against the live env:

    1. **`sprk_regardingreportcard` lookup on `sprk_communication`** — confirm the regarding lookup exists (target = the report-card entity) with its exact logical name; task 010 adds the `RegardingFieldMap.cs` entry that writes it.
    2. **`sprk_recordtype_ref` RPTC row + `sprk_reportcardnumber`** — confirm a `sprk_recordtype_ref` row exists for the report-card record type (RPTC), and that the number field the identifier rung reverse-looks-up against (`sprk_reportcardnumber` or the value in that row's `sprk_regardingrecordnumberfield`) is present. Capture the row's `sprk_regardingfield` + `sprk_regardingrecordnumberfield` values verbatim.
    3. **`sprk_emailupdatefield` table (Job B allow-list, FR-11)** — confirm the table exists with the FR-11 columns: `sprk_targetentity` (→ `sprk_recordtype_ref`), `sprk_targetfield`, `sprk_enabled`, `sprk_fieldtype`, `sprk_requireconfirm`, `sprk_extractionguidance`. Record any starter allow-list rows present. Phase 3 (Job B) is GATED on this table existing.
    4. **`sprk_recordtype_ref` roster (7 core record types) + data-hygiene** — enumerate the rows for the 7 core records (matter, project, invoice, work assignment, budget, service request, report card). For EACH capture `sprk_regardingfield` + `sprk_regardingrecordnumberfield` verbatim. Flag the KNOWN data-hygiene issues explicitly: **typos in some `sprk_regardingfield` values** and the **`contact`-row anomaly**. Produce a "read-defensively" map that task 020 uses (which field names are trustworthy, which need normalization/guarding).

    Do NOT mutate schema, do NOT write code. The single deliverable is the findings note (the confirmed presence/absence of each input + the verbatim `sprk_recordtype_ref` roster + the defensive-read typo/anomaly map).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke Dataverse schema-verification engineer. Fluent in the Dataverse MCP read tools (`describe`, `read_query`, `search`), the `sprk_recordtype_ref` catalog contract (codes + regarding fields + number fields), and the `Services/Communication/**` association-engine layout. You confirm ground truth and hand tasks 010/020/030 an exact, do-not-assume delta — you add nothing and change nothing live.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A findings note exists under `projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/notes/` recording: (a) `sprk_regardingreportcard` lookup present on `sprk_communication` with its exact logical name (for 010); (b) the `sprk_recordtype_ref` RPTC row present with `sprk_reportcardnumber` / its number-field value (for 020's roster); (c) `sprk_emailupdatefield` present with the FR-11 columns + any seed rows (gates Phase 3); (d) the 7-record `sprk_recordtype_ref` roster verbatim PLUS a "read-defensively" map of `sprk_regardingfield` typos and the `contact`-row anomaly that task 020 must guard against. Tasks 010/020/030 can build against ground truth. No schema or code changed. If ANY required input is missing, the note states it explicitly and flags the blocked downstream task (010/020 blocked on 1/2; Phase 3 blocked on 3).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      r1 builds the intelligence + record-write spine over the shipped communication engine (r4). Four schema inputs are OPERATOR-created (not r1 tasks): the `sprk_regardingreportcard` lookup, the `sprk_recordtype_ref` RPTC row + `sprk_reportcardnumber`, the `sprk_emailupdatefield` allow-list table, and the `sprk_recordtype_ref` catalog whose codes + number fields the identifier rung (020) reads. This spike verifies those exist LIVE before the dependent tasks run (plan §4). The recurring failure mode is building against an assumed schema shape; the second is trusting a `sprk_recordtype_ref` catalog that has known typos in some `sprk_regardingfield` values and a `contact`-row anomaly (spec §Dependencies → Prerequisites; CLAUDE.md Phase 0). Task 020 must read the catalog defensively (or the operator cleans it first) — this note produces the exact typo/anomaly map so 020 can guard deterministically.

      This is a verification spike (verify-before-build), not new surface — no §11 Component Justification is required (it introduces no component; it changes nothing live).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/spec.md (FR-11, §Dependencies → Prerequisites — the four operator inputs + the data-hygiene note)</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/plan.md §4 (External Prerequisites table — what each input gates)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/RegardingFieldMap.cs (the regarding write map task 010 extends; the report-card entry it will add reads `sprk_regardingreportcard`)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/Rungs/ExplicitReferenceRung.cs (the rung 0 pattern task 020 clones; it reads `sprk_recordtype_ref` roster + number fields)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">READ-ONLY. This spike MUST NOT create, update, or delete any Dataverse attribute/entity/option-set and MUST NOT modify any code. The single deliverable is a findings note.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec §Dependencies">Confirm the `sprk_recordtype_ref` `sprk_regardingfield` typos + the `contact`-row anomaly explicitly, and produce a "read-defensively" map (trustworthy vs needs-normalization field names) that task 020 consumes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec FR-11">Confirm `sprk_emailupdatefield` exists with the FR-11 columns (`sprk_targetentity`→`sprk_recordtype_ref`, `sprk_targetfield`, `sprk_enabled`, `sprk_fieldtype`, `sprk_requireconfirm`, `sprk_extractionguidance`). Phase 3 (Job B) is gated on this table existing; if absent, flag Phase 3 blocked.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Use Dataverse MCP read tools (`describe`/`read_query`/`search`) for live schema; capture `sprk_recordtype_ref` roster field values verbatim. Do NOT guess field names from memory.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Gates 010 (needs `sprk_regardingreportcard` + RPTC row), 020 (needs the roster + defensive-read map), and Phase 3 (needs `sprk_emailupdatefield`) — the note MUST be specific enough that each builds with zero assumption. If an input is missing, name the blocked task.</constraint>
  </constraints>

