  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read spec FR-11 + §Dependencies (the four operator inputs + the data-hygiene note) + plan §4 to fix exactly which inputs each downstream task needs and what "read defensively" means.</step>
    <step order="2">MCP `describe` `sprk_communication`: confirm the `sprk_regardingreportcard` lookup exists (target + exact logical name) for task 010.</step>
    <step order="3">MCP `read_query` `sprk_recordtype_ref`: confirm the RPTC (report-card) row exists; capture its `sprk_regardingfield` + `sprk_regardingrecordnumberfield` verbatim; confirm the `sprk_reportcardnumber` number field is present on the report-card entity.</step>
    <step order="4">MCP `describe` `sprk_emailupdatefield`: confirm the table exists with the FR-11 columns; `read_query` any seed allow-list rows. If the table is absent, record it and flag Phase 3 (030/031) blocked.</step>
    <step order="5">MCP `read_query` the `sprk_recordtype_ref` rows for the 7 core record types; capture each row's `sprk_regardingfield` + `sprk_regardingrecordnumberfield` verbatim; flag the known `sprk_regardingfield` typos + the `contact`-row anomaly; build the "read-defensively" map (trustworthy vs needs-normalization) for task 020.</step>
    <step order="6">Write the findings note `projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/notes/001-operator-schema-verification.md`: (a) `sprk_regardingreportcard` present + logical name; (b) RPTC row + number field; (c) `sprk_emailupdatefield` present + columns + seed rows (or ABSENT → Phase 3 blocked); (d) the 7-record roster verbatim + the defensive-read typo/anomaly map. State per-input PRESENT/ABSENT and name any blocked downstream task.</step>
    <step order="7">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (001 ✅) + `current-task.md`; confirm 010/011/012/013/020/022 unblocked (or flag which are blocked on a missing input) and point them at the note.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="read">Spec + plan + `RegardingFieldMap.cs` + `ExplicitReferenceRung.cs`</tool>
    <tool name="mcp-dataverse-describe">Live `sprk_communication` / `sprk_emailupdatefield` attribute enumeration (read-only)</tool>
    <tool name="mcp-dataverse-read_query">`sprk_recordtype_ref` roster rows + `sprk_emailupdatefield` seed rows (read-only)</tool>
    <tool name="write">The findings note under `notes/`</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="docs">projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/notes/001-operator-schema-verification.md (per-input PRESENT/ABSENT + `sprk_regardingreportcard` logical name + RPTC row/number field + `sprk_emailupdatefield` columns/seed + verbatim 7-record `sprk_recordtype_ref` roster + defensive-read typo/anomaly map + any blocked-task flags)</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md (status update 001 ✅)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The note confirms whether `sprk_regardingreportcard` exists on `sprk_communication` and records its exact logical name + target (for task 010).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The note confirms whether the `sprk_recordtype_ref` RPTC row exists and captures its `sprk_regardingfield` + `sprk_regardingrecordnumberfield` + the `sprk_reportcardnumber` field (for task 020's roster).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The note confirms whether `sprk_emailupdatefield` exists with the FR-11 columns (`sprk_targetentity`, `sprk_targetfield`, `sprk_enabled`, `sprk_fieldtype`, `sprk_requireconfirm`, `sprk_extractionguidance`) and records seed rows; if absent, it flags Phase 3 (030/031) blocked.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The note enumerates the 7-core-record `sprk_recordtype_ref` roster verbatim (`sprk_regardingfield` + `sprk_regardingrecordnumberfield` per row) and produces a read-defensively map naming the `sprk_regardingfield` typos + the `contact`-row anomaly for task 020.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: no Dataverse attribute/entity/option-set was created, updated, or deleted, and no source code was modified — this task changed nothing live (read-only verification).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: the note does NOT assume any input is present — every one of the four inputs is stated PRESENT or ABSENT from a live MCP read, and any ABSENT input names the blocked downstream task.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Gates Phase 1 (010/011/012/013) and the identifier rung (020) + Phase 3 (Job B, gated on `sprk_emailupdatefield`). Do NOT skip the live MCP read in favor of trusting the spec's prerequisite list — the list is the hypothesis; this task confirms it against the deployed env. The defensive-read typo/anomaly map is the single most load-bearing deliverable for 020 (bad roster → wrong reverse-lookup → misfiling).
  </notes>

